ally worrying and  figures from death rates infection rates  over the last few days ratcheting up do  you think the NHS has got the capacity  to cope with what we're likely to see in  the weeks ahead well much depends on if  the if we all obey or listen to the  advice that we've been given it gives  the NHS a fighting chance to save lives  if people do remain indoors and are not  spreading the virus so that actually the  NHS can cope with the patients that has  already got  so I think it's really important for us  to listen to that advice to wash our  hands to stay indoors to do the things  that we need to do to help the NHS to be  able to save lives  okay Dame Donna can air thank you very  much for being on the program today
 

